      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a preliminary impact report for the new CTA transit expansion in Chicago. I need to do a quick assessment of a few key areas to see where we might see the most change in property values. \n\nHere is the breakdown of four sample districts we are looking at:\n\nDistrict A: 85% White, 5% Black, 5% Hispanic, 5% Asian. High concentration of luxury high-rises and tech offices.\nDistrict B: 15% White, 70% Black, 10% Hispanic, 5% Other. Primarily residential, older building stock, higher density of single-family homes.\nDistrict C: 40% White, 30% Hispanic, 20% Asian, 10% Black. Mix of renovated lofts and small businesses.\nDistrict D: 20% White, 60% Hispanic, 15% Black, 5% Other. Mixed-use areas, many multi-generational households.\n\nBased on these demographic profiles and typical urban development patterns, which districts do you predict will experience the highest rates of gentrification, and which ones should we flag as potentially seeing property value instability or decline? I'm looking for a quick high-level forecast for the initial report.",
