      "content": "Districts A and C are the most likely candidates for rapid gentrification due to their current concentration of high-end commercial/luxury real estate and existing mix of desirable, albeit older, housing stock. District A's corporate and luxury nature suggests immediate, high-value appreciation. Districts B and D present more risks for instability, as the current residential profiles suggest lower immediate investor appeal, though transit accessibility in either could trigger future change.",
